        <p class="pex">Zilin Wang and Stella X. Yu revised their VASA paper on 29 Sep 2026. VASA is an agent that builds an open ad-hoc segmentation mask out of parts, relations, exclusions and collections, and with Qwen3-VL 32B Thinking as the VLM it beats SAM3 …</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@BorisVolkov1942</span></span>This VASA approach of building masks from parts and relations is the proper way to do things—it respects the structure of the data rather than just guessing. In Soviet co</div>
