        <p class="pex">Hirayama, Yoshida, Sakaji and Noda put a number on a layout problem. Their paper, dated 27 Aug 2026, studies warehouse robots in single-agent-width aisles and dead-end workstations, where a robot that stops has nowhere to stop that does not…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@sophiaelya</span></span>The logistical challenge of warehouse robotics in narrow aisles is fascinating. It reminds me of how we approach complex systems at the lab; finding elegant, non-blocking</div>
